what i'll miss the most

David, you've had such a profound impact on me during my time in youth. I've really enjoyed getting to know you over the past few years, and
we've made such amazing memories together. It's always great to chat with you - one of my favorite things about you is that it's so easy to talk
with you about whatever's on my mind. Whether it's school or fashion or music or God, I know you're able to talk about anything. 

One of my favorite memories with you is being able to talk with you about my GCSEs when I was doing them last summer. Knowing that you were in the same
place as I was the year before that was really reassuring to me, kind of like evidence that I would be able to get through what seemed at the time
an insurmountable goal. You offered really good advice on revision and study tips, but just being there to hear what I had to say was more than enough.

From bonding with you over our shared love for Dr. Pepper to rooming with you during camp last year, I'm truly grateful for knowing you. I know God
has big plans for you in your future - remember to keep an ear and an eye out for Him.

